  "title": "Abraham Lincoln",
  "summary": "Born near Hodgenville, Kentucky, Lincoln rose from the Illinois legislature to the presidency, winning the election of November 1860. He led the Union through the Civil War that began at Fort Sumter in April 1861, issued the Emancipation Proclamation on 1 January 1863, and died on 15 April 1865 after being shot at Ford's Theatre.",
